Discussion: OpenRune/OpenRune-Server#353

From our per-feature patches `47-achievement-diary-journals`, `49-achievement-diary-areas-and-progress`, `53-diary-task-hooks-lumbridge-varrock` (in [`openrune/upstream/`](https://github.com/AlexPerrin/osrs-plugins-reverse/tree/main/openrune/upstream) of osrs-plugins-reverse), applied with `git am` on `main` (`1be5dfb5f`); commits kept as they are except for the `feat:`/`fix:` subject.

Three commits, one per patch, each on the one before.

**Build status: this branch does not pass all checks** (cache build pass, `spotlessCheck` **FAIL**, `assemble test integration` pass, boot: Server ready in 7.093000459s). Details under Tests.

**Problem.** Open <area> Journal in the Achievement Diaries tab did nothing, and no diary task progress was tracked.

**Change.** New modules `content/interfaces/achievement-diary` + pack:
- **Journals (47, 49):** the journal scroll (741) with each area's tasks per tier, word-wrapped by p12 widths, for all 12 areas. RuneLite's Diary Requirements plugin annotates these lines (checked on a client).
- **Progress (49, 53):** 31 Lumbridge & Draynor / Varrock tasks drive the client's diary count varbits and strike done tasks in the journal, through one-line hooks in existing content (Hans, sawmill, cooking, firemaking, teleports, runecrafting, essence mine, thieving, crafting, Thessalia, Gertrude, the Stronghold of Security, slayer masters, the canoe...).

**Tests.** `DiaryTasksTest` (integration).

On this branch (Docker `eclipse-temurin:21`, upstream's `./gradlew`, a clean `freshCache` of main restored first, then `:or-cache:buildCache :or-cache:mergePluginGamevals`; `assemble`, `test` and `integration` as separate runs in a 4 GB container): cache build pass, `spotlessCheck` **FAIL**, `assemble test integration` pass, boot: Server ready in 7.093000459s.

`spotlessCheck` fails on formatting only, in 17 files of 13 modules (`spotlessApply` fixes it): the `DiaryHooks` / `PlayEmote` / `VarPlayerIntMapSetter` imports that patches 49 and 53 add are out of ktlint's lexicographic order (added at the top of each import block), and two stray blank lines. The commits are kept as the patches are; the fix belongs in the patches before anything goes upstream. Compile, tests and boot pass.

Nothing was checked in game from this exact branch; in-game checks mentioned above were on our own server build (main's pin `9a8b338a8` plus these and our other patches).

**Data sources.** Wiki-derived data or text (OSRS Wiki, by the wiki's contributors, CC BY-NC-SA 3.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/3.0/; OpenRune is ISC): the task lists of the journals (the Diary Requirements plugin's wording where it has one). See question 4 in #353 on how upstream wants to handle that.

**Caveats.**
- Per-task bits are in server varps 63976-63984 and 63160; the real `*_achievement_diary` bit layout is not mapped.
- No task-complete chat message (wording unknown); title and tier heading wording are guesses; area boxes (Lumbridge, the Al Kharid mine, others) are approximate.
- Conflict resolved when applying on main: in `CookingEvents.kt` the hook is added after main's own success message (the original patch's context had a reworded message from another of our patches, not in this branch).
- Touches several content modules' build files for the hook dependency.

**Release note.** Achievement diary journals for all areas, with Lumbridge & Draynor and Varrock task progress.

